e-governance walkthrough log — 2026-10-10
Worked-case lesson: no command line by design (brief §6).
The "run" is the governance charter authored and self-reviewed in-session
against NIST CSF 2.0's Govern function (CSWP 29, Feb 26 2024; PDF fetched
2026-10-10, 1,518,858 bytes).

Scope: fictional Copperline Freight (240 staff, 3 sites, regional logistics;
newly hired CISO, no charter, security budget as IT overhead, no risk
committee). Charter elements authored: mission alignment statement (protect
dispatch availability / shipment-data confidentiality / customer trust);
CISO reports to CEO with quarterly board slot (old CISO-under-CIO failure
corrected in writing); quarterly risk committee (CEO, CFO, CIO, CISO, GC);
board-approved risk appetite (absolute at center: no unmitigated risk to
dispatch or customer data); framework rationale (CSF 2.0 as program language —
outcomes-based, free, board-readable; ISO 27001 deferred with review date;
SOC 2 Type II scoped to the tracking portal only); policy authority + exception
path (requester, risk statement, approver, expiry); AI governance assigned to
CISO with risk-committee review for customer-affecting AI; oversight cadence
(quarterly metrics, annual charter review).

Self-review checklist (2026-10-10):
